==Battleground==
*4 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Loris]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns.
**1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns.
**6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns.
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
**1 [[General GreGory]] spawns.
**8 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
**1 [[Metal One Horn]] spawns.
**1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The biggest danger here is at the start. The Sir Rels are deadly dangerous and can easily overpower a weak defense. To make matters worse there's only a 10 second window in which to generate enough money to be ready for battle. Maximum level erasers are a minimum requirement, along with a damage dealer cheap and powerful enough to take them down quickly at the start. If your cats can't take down the Sir Rels before they begin to stack then it's almost certainly game over.

[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] (or [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]) is superb in this role if well shielded. It's relatively cheap and has very powerful single target damage. That's why stalling to build the wallet is not an option except perhaps for the last of the initial four Sir Rels. Once the four Sir Rels at the start are dealt with and the enemy base is hit, the battle really begins. At this point the only significant requirement is to maintain a strong frontline that can withstand the Sir Rels at all times, if they break through at any point it's not going to end well.

In addition you must bring something that can perform a [[Critical Hit]] reliably or Metal One Horn will completely ruin your day. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] is the obvious candidate.

